Date:   Fri Sep 25 22:21:22 2026 +1000

    KS-1263: make /share and /transfer-custody's multi-writes one transaction, via withTenant (#1239)
    
    The route-level rollback cell injects its failure with a NUL byte that production refuses before reaching the route, and it runs as a superuser because its harness omits the tenant-scope middleware; the rollback it proves holds regardless, and was re-measured red at develop and green at head as the app role inside that middleware. The custody-transfer rollback is pinned by structure and by a direct transaction cell, not yet by a committed route cell. The integration suite cannot run in single-tenant mode on a fresh worktree and fails loudly by name there.
    
    12/15 ran; legs 3, 4, 8 NOT run (local stack not up); no such surface
    
    Merged by Seat B 27th on Wednesday's signed GO (2026-09-25T12:17:23Z) naming head c8e1875c21e9, under Kam's open-ended TESTED grant of 2026-09-11 (gate tier-1 gate21T1d, report sha256 86dbbcab1585). Round 1 and the first half of round 2 were written by the previous seat, which wrapped; this seat completed round 2 (the route-level rollback cell and the transaction-client identity assertion) and the head merged here is therefore this seat's own commit. Recorded rather than left to be inferred.
    
    Refs KS-1263
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

